e, not an unimportant one; the arrangements still belong in this diary.","I thought background meant something that could have no effect on the activities described.","I would count only unusual online events, leaving out the repeated uses that organise the day."]},"advanced-native-1976-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Online communication may be part of the background of modern childhood, but our exhibition welcomes different records of daily arrangements, including paper schedules. Please choose something you are willing to share and remove personal details rather than feel required to submit a screenshot.","To explore what is part of the background of modern childhood, we invite families to contribute a record of an ordinary day in a form that suits them. A paper timetable is as welcome as an edited message extract, and participation is optional."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
