('advanced-native-2009', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2009-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The awards remained valuable, but current reporting and corrections were still needed."],"options":["The awards remained valuable, but current reporting and corrections were still needed.","The speaker said the old awards had never represented any worthwhile work.","Repeating the prize list was presented as enough to check each new local claim.","The paper had already closed and the account concerned only its final sale."]},"advanced-native-2009-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["A prize list could record past achievement without answering current readers’ questions.","It could not live on reputation alone; readers needed evidence of present care.","Old awards did not check the facts in each new article.","Trust needed support from what the paper was doing now."],"options":["A prize list could record past achievement without answering current readers’ questions.","It could not live on reputation alone; readers needed evidence of present care.","Old awards did not check the facts in each new article.","Trust needed support from what the paper was doing now."]},"advanced-native-2009-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Having a reputation does not show that the shop is trying to live on reputation alone when current careful work is described."],"options":["Having a reputation does not show that the shop is trying to live on reputation alone when current careful work is described.","Mentioning its history establishes that the shop no longer checks new repairs.","The checks took place only when the shop first earned its reputation, not on the newly delivered items."]},"advanced-native-2009-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Treat past prestige as a substitute for asking whether the present work meets people’s needs."],"options":["Treat past prestige as a substitute for asking whether the present work meets people’s needs.","Identify what present action would support